Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 20:44:55 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] loc: add BeiDou to QmiLocSystem

A SM7150 modem reports satellites with system 6, which the enum does not
cover, so they came out as unknown. They are BeiDou: their satellite ids sit
in the 201-237 range that QMI LOC uses for BeiDou, and at the same time the
modem's own NMEA reports a GSA with system id 4, which is BeiDou in NMEA
4.10. COMPASS (4) is the older name and is left alone.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/libqmi-glib/qmi-enums-loc.h | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/libqmi-glib/qmi-enums-loc.h b/src/libqmi-glib/qmi-enums-loc.h
index 6c7e623..6366b01 100644
--- a/src/libqmi-glib/qmi-enums-loc.h
+++ b/src/libqmi-glib/qmi-enums-loc.h
@@ -279,6 +279,7 @@ typedef enum { /*< since=1.22 >*/
  * @QMI_LOC_SYSTEM_SBAS: SBAS.
  * @QMI_LOC_SYSTEM_COMPASS: COMPASS (BeiDou).
  * @QMI_LOC_SYSTEM_GLONASS: GLONASS.
+ * @QMI_LOC_SYSTEM_BDS: BeiDou. Since 1.39.
  *
  * Which location system a satellite is part of.
  *
@@ -290,6 +291,7 @@ typedef enum { /*< since=1.22 >*/
     QMI_LOC_SYSTEM_SBAS    = 3,
     QMI_LOC_SYSTEM_COMPASS = 4,
     QMI_LOC_SYSTEM_GLONASS = 5,
+    QMI_LOC_SYSTEM_BDS     = 6,
 } QmiLocSystem;
 
